# Notes
notes = "(!) sega_101.bin (md5): f273555d7d91e8a5a6bfd9bcf066331c|(!) sega_100.bin (md5): 2aba43c2f1526c5e898dfe1cafbfc53a|Built on Ymir's cycle-accurate hardware layer (verbatim upstream).|Requires one Saturn BIOS ROM (place in system directory); any of the listed files works.|Load .bin/.img/.mdf images through their .cue/.ccd/.mds sheet.|Japanese BIOS files (Sega Saturn BIOS v1.00/v1.01 (JAP).bin) are also supported.|Note: sega1003.bin (JP v1.003) is NOT supported due to compatibility issues.|Visit https://github.com/coredds/brimir for more information."

description = "Brimir is a libretro core for Sega Saturn emulation, built on Ymir's cycle-accurate hardware layer. Features SIMD-optimized threaded software rendering, live core option updates, dynamic NTSC/PAL AV timing, SRAM single-source persistence, screen rotation (TATE), compressed versioned save states, and multi-disc support. Ymir's hardware layer stays verbatim upstream; Brimir features are implemented in the bridge layer. Interlaced high-resolution titles can be CPU-bound on slower machines. Active development targets cheat support, all Saturn controller types, RetroAchievements, and an SH-2 JIT. The core requires a Saturn BIOS ROM to function."
